## Performance Comparison

| Operation | Scalar | SSE (4x) | AVX (8x) | NEON (4x) |
|-----------|--------|----------|----------|-----------|
| Multiply-add | 1x | 4x | 8x | 4x |
| Biquad filter | 1x | 3.5x | 7x | 3.5x |
| FFT (N=1024) | 1x | 3x | 6x | 3x |
| Convolution | 1x | 3x | 5x | 3x |

## Common Pitfalls

1. **Alignment**: SIMD requires aligned memory for best performance
```cpp
alignas(16) float buffer[1024];  // SSE aligned
alignas(32) float buffer[1024];  // AVX aligned
```

2. **Remainder handling**: Process non-SIMD-aligned samples separately
```cpp
int remainder = numSamples % simdSize;
for (int i = numSamples - remainder; i < numSamples; ++i)
{
    // Scalar processing for remainder
}
```

3. **Data layout**: Interleaved vs planar affects SIMD efficiency

4. **Compiler optimization**: Use appropriate flags (-mavx, -msse4.2, etc.)

## Best Practices

| Practice | Benefit |
|----------|--------|
| Align buffers | Avoid unaligned loads |
| Batch processing | Amortize overhead |
| SIMD-aware API | Clean code path |
| Fallback path | Compatibility |
| Runtime dispatch | Best performance per CPU |

